IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `coa-core`

-- coa18-part22-interest.l4: Companies Act 2006 (United Kingdom), Part 22, ss 820 to 828: the meaning of "interest in
-- shares" (ss 820 to 825), the supplementary provisions (ss 826 to 828), and the reckoning of periods in working days
-- (s 827). Lines 11035-11118 of ukpga-2006-46.txt. Layer 1: the law, objectively.
-- How to read an answer (JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE, NOTHING), the gate of s 791 and the seams are as in the header of
-- coa18-part22-notice.l4.
--
-- NO GATHERING (ruling E1, option C). ss 820 to 825 each answer for themselves: a caller who asks "does the person have an
-- interest in the shares" asks each section and takes any JUST TRUE; this module does not gather the routes into one answer.
-- DEEMING. Where a provision says a person "is treated as" or "is taken to be" interested, JUST TRUE is the provision's effect;
-- where the text introduces the limbs with "if" or "where" a failed limb is JUST FALSE for that provision (marginal reading
-- (a)); where it does not, the case outside the provision's own words is NOTHING.

§ `Part 22 (ss 791 to 828), third module: ss 820 to 828`

§§ `s 820 Interest in shares: general`

-- src:11036 | 820 Interest in shares: general
-- src:11037 | (1) This section applies to determine for the purposes of this Part whether a person has an interest in shares.
@ref s 820(1) Interest in shares: general (src:11036-11037)
GIVEN `the question is whether a person has an interest in shares for the purposes of this Part` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 820(1) this section applies to determine whether the person has an interest in the shares` MEANS
    IF `the question is whether a person has an interest in shares for the purposes of this Part`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section applies to determine for the purposes of this Part whether a person has an interest in shares."

-- src:11038 | (2) In this Part—
-- src:11039 | (a) a reference to an interest in shares includes an interest of any kind whatsoever in the shares, and
-- src:11040 | (b) any restraints or restrictions to which the exercise of any right attached to the interest is or may be subject shall be disregarded.
@ref s 820(2)(a) Interest in shares: general (src:11038-11040)
GIVEN `the person has an interest of any kind whatsoever in the shares` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 820(2)(a) the person has an interest in the shares` MEANS
    IF `the person has an interest of any kind whatsoever in the shares`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "a reference to an interest in shares includes an interest of any kind whatsoever in the shares" does not close the meaning

@ref s 820(2)(b) Interest in shares: general (src:11040-11040)
GIVEN `there is a restraint or restriction to which the exercise of a right attached to the interest is or may be subject` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 820(2)(b) the restraint or restriction is disregarded` MEANS
    IF `there is a restraint or restriction to which the exercise of a right attached to the interest is or may be subject`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any restraints or restrictions to which the exercise of any right attached to the interest is or may be subject shall be disregarded": there is nothing to disregard

-- src:11041 | (3) Where an interest in shares is comprised in property held on trust, every beneficiary of the trust is treated as having an interest in the shares.
@ref s 820(3) Interest in shares: general (src:11041-11041)
GIVEN `an interest in shares is comprised in property held on trust` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a beneficiary of the trust` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 820(3) the person is treated as having an interest in the shares` MEANS
    IF `an interest in shares is comprised in property held on trust` AND `the person is a beneficiary of the trust`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where an interest in shares is comprised in property held on trust, every beneficiary of the trust is treated as having an interest in the shares."

-- src:11042 | (4) A person is treated as having an interest in shares if—
-- src:11043 | (a) he enters into a contract to acquire them, or
-- src:11044 | (b) not being the registered holder, he is entitled—
-- src:11045 | (i) to exercise any right conferred by the holding of the shares, or
-- src:11046 | (ii) to control the exercise of any such right.
@ref s 820(4) Interest in shares: general (src:11042-11046)
GIVEN `the person enters into a contract to acquire the shares` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is the registered holder of the shares` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is entitled to exercise a right conferred by the holding of the shares` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is entitled to control the exercise of such a right` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 820(4) the person is treated as having an interest in the shares` MEANS
    IF     `the person enters into a contract to acquire the shares`
        OR (    (NOT `the person is the registered holder of the shares`)
            AND (   `the person is entitled to exercise a right conferred by the holding of the shares`
                 OR `the person is entitled to control the exercise of such a right`))
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A person is treated as having an interest in shares if— (a) he enters into a contract to acquire them, or (b) not being the registered holder, he is entitled— (i) to exercise any right conferred by the holding of the shares, or (ii) to control the exercise of any such right."

-- src:11047 | (5) For the purposes of subsection (4)(b) a person is entitled to exercise or control the exercise of a right conferred by the holding of shares if he—
-- src:11048 | (a) has a right (whether subject to conditions or not) the exercise of which would make him so entitled, or
-- src:11049 | (b) is under an obligation (whether subject to conditions or not) the fulfilment of which would make him so entitled.
@ref s 820(5) Interest in shares: general (src:11047-11049)
GIVEN `the person has a right (whether subject to conditions or not) the exercise of which would make him so entitled` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is under an obligation (whether subject to conditions or not) the fulfilment of which would make him so entitled` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 820(5) the person is entitled to exercise or control the exercise of a right conferred by the holding of shares` MEANS
    IF     `the person has a right (whether subject to conditions or not) the exercise of which would make him so entitled`
        OR `the person is under an obligation (whether subject to conditions or not) the fulfilment of which would make him so entitled`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "For the purposes of subsection (4)(b) a person is entitled to exercise or control the exercise of a right conferred by the holding of shares if he— (a) has a right ... or (b) is under an obligation ..."

-- src:11050 | (6) A person is treated as having an interest in shares if—
-- src:11051 | (a) he has a right to call for delivery of the shares to himself or to his order, or
-- src:11052 | (b) he has a right to acquire an interest in shares or is under an obligation to take an interest in shares.
-- src:11053 | This applies whether the right or obligation is conditional or absolute.
@ref s 820(6) Interest in shares: general (src:11050-11053)
GIVEN `the person has a right to call for delivery of the shares to himself or to his order` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has a right to acquire an interest in shares` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is under an obligation to take an interest in shares` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 820(6) the person is treated as having an interest in shares` MEANS
    IF     `the person has a right to call for delivery of the shares to himself or to his order`
        OR `the person has a right to acquire an interest in shares`
        OR `the person is under an obligation to take an interest in shares`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A person is treated as having an interest in shares if— (a) he has a right to call for delivery of the shares to himself or to his order, or (b) he has a right to acquire an interest in shares or is under an obligation to take an interest in shares."

-- (6), last sentence: "This applies whether the right or obligation is conditional or absolute." Either way (6) applies.
@ref s 820(6) Interest in shares: general (src:11053-11053)
GIVEN `the right or obligation is conditional` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 820(6) it is immaterial whether the right or obligation is conditional or absolute` MEANS
    IF `the right or obligation is conditional`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST TRUE

-- src:11054 | (7) Persons having a joint interest are treated as each having that interest.
@ref s 820(7) Interest in shares: general (src:11054-11054)
GIVEN `the persons have a joint interest` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 820(7) the persons are treated as each having that interest` MEANS
    IF `the persons have a joint interest`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Persons having a joint interest are treated as each having that interest."

-- src:11055 | (8) It is immaterial that shares in which a person has an interest are unidentifiable.
@ref s 820(8) Interest in shares: general (src:11055-11055)
GIVEN `the shares in which the person has an interest are unidentifiable` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 820(8) it is immaterial that the shares are unidentifiable` MEANS
    IF `the shares in which the person has an interest are unidentifiable`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "It is immaterial that shares in which a person has an interest are unidentifiable.": identifiable shares are not mentioned

§§ `s 821 Interest in shares: right to subscribe for shares`

-- src:11057 | (1) Section 793 (notice by company requiring information about interests in its shares) applies in relation to a person who has, or previously had, or is or was entitled to acquire, a right to subscribe for shares in the company as it applies in relation to a person who is or was interested in shares in that company.
@ref s 821(1) Interest in shares: right to subscribe for shares (src:11057-11057)
GIVEN `the person has, or previously had, or is or was entitled to acquire, a right to subscribe for shares in the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 821(1) section 793 applies in relation to the person as it applies to a person who is or was interested in shares` MEANS
    IF `the person has, or previously had, or is or was entitled to acquire, a right to subscribe for shares in the company`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Section 793 ... applies in relation to a person who has, or previously had, or is or was entitled to acquire, a right to subscribe for shares in the company"

-- src:11058 | (2) References in that section to an interest in shares shall be read accordingly.
@ref s 821(2) Interest in shares: right to subscribe for shares (src:11058-11058)
GIVEN `the person has, or previously had, or is or was entitled to acquire, a right to subscribe for shares in the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 821(2) references in section 793 to an interest in shares are read as including the right to subscribe` MEANS
    IF `the person has, or previously had, or is or was entitled to acquire, a right to subscribe for shares in the company`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "References in that section to an interest in shares shall be read accordingly": only in relation to a person within subsection (1)

§§ `s 822 Interest in shares: family interests`

-- src:11060 | (1) For the purposes of this Part a person is taken to be interested in shares in which—
-- src:11061 | (a) his spouse or civil partner, or
-- src:11062 | (b) any infant child or step-child of his,
-- src:11063 | is interested.
@ref s 822(1) Interest in shares: family interests (src:11060-11063)
GIVEN `the person's spouse or civil partner is interested in the shares` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an infant child or step-child of the person is interested in the shares` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 822(1) the person is taken to be interested in the shares` MEANS
    IF `the person's spouse or civil partner is interested in the shares` OR `an infant child or step-child of the person is interested in the shares`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a person is taken to be interested in shares in which— (a) his spouse or civil partner, or (b) any infant child or step-child of his, is interested"

-- (2): in relation to Scotland "infant" means a person under 18; elsewhere the Act does not define it in this Part.
-- src:11064 | (2) In relation to Scotland “infant” means a person under the age of 18 years.
@ref s 822(2) Interest in shares: family interests (src:11064-11064)
GIVEN `the part of the United Kingdom concerned` IS A `Place of registration`
      `the person's age in years` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 822(2) the person is an infant` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the part of the United Kingdom concerned`
    WHEN `Scotland` THEN
        IF `the person's age in years` LESS THAN 18
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "In relation to Scotland “infant” means a person under the age of 18 years."
    OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In relation to Scotland": the meaning elsewhere is not given in this Part

§§ `s 823 Interest in shares: corporate interests`

-- src:11066 | (1) For the purposes of this Part a person is taken to be interested in shares if a body corporate is interested in them and—
-- src:11067 | (a) the body or its directors are accustomed to act in accordance with his directions or instructions, or
-- src:11068 | (b) he is entitled to exercise or control the exercise of one-third or more of the voting power at general meetings of the body.
@ref s 823(1) Interest in shares: corporate interests (src:11066-11068)
GIVEN `a body corporate is interested in the shares` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the body or its directors are accustomed to act in accordance with the person's directions or instructions` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the fraction of the voting power at general meetings of the body that the person is entitled to exercise or control the exercise of` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 823(1) the person is taken to be interested in the shares` MEANS
    IF     `a body corporate is interested in the shares`
       AND (   `the body or its directors are accustomed to act in accordance with the person's directions or instructions`
            OR `the fraction of the voting power at general meetings of the body that the person is entitled to exercise or control the exercise of` AT LEAST (1 DIVIDED BY 3))
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a person is taken to be interested in shares if a body corporate is interested in them and— (a) the body or its directors are accustomed to act in accordance with his directions or instructions, or (b) he is entitled to exercise or control the exercise of one-third or more of the voting power at general meetings of the body."

-- src:11069 | (2) For the purposes of this section a person is treated as entitled to exercise or control the exercise of voting power if—
-- src:11070 | (a) another body corporate is entitled to exercise or control the exercise of that voting power, and
-- src:11071 | (b) he is entitled to exercise or control the exercise of one-third or more of the voting power at general meetings of that body corporate.
@ref s 823(2) Interest in shares: corporate interests (src:11069-11071)
GIVEN `another body corporate is entitled to exercise or control the exercise of that voting power` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the fraction of the voting power at general meetings of that body corporate that the person is entitled to exercise or control the exercise of` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 823(2) the person is treated as entitled to exercise or control the exercise of the voting power` MEANS
    IF     `another body corporate is entitled to exercise or control the exercise of that voting power`
       AND `the fraction of the voting power at general meetings of that body corporate that the person is entitled to exercise or control the exercise of` AT LEAST (1 DIVIDED BY 3)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a person is treated as entitled to exercise or control the exercise of voting power if— (a) another body corporate is entitled ..., and (b) he is entitled to exercise or control the exercise of one-third or more of the voting power at general meetings of that body corporate."

-- src:11072 | (3) For the purposes of this section a person is treated as entitled to exercise or control the exercise of voting power if—
-- src:11073 | (a) he has a right (whether or not subject to conditions) the exercise of which would make him so entitled, or
-- src:11074 | (b) he is under an obligation (whether or not subject to conditions) the fulfilment of which would make him so entitled.
@ref s 823(3) Interest in shares: corporate interests (src:11072-11074)
GIVEN `the person has a right (whether or not subject to conditions) the exercise of which would make him so entitled` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is under an obligation (whether or not subject to conditions) the fulfilment of which would make him so entitled` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 823(3) the person is treated as entitled to exercise or control the exercise of the voting power` MEANS
    IF     `the person has a right (whether or not subject to conditions) the exercise of which would make him so entitled`
        OR `the person is under an obligation (whether or not subject to conditions) the fulfilment of which would make him so entitled`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a person is treated as entitled to exercise or control the exercise of voting power if— (a) he has a right ... or (b) he is under an obligation ..."

§§ `s 824 Interest in shares: agreement to acquire interests in a particular company`

-- src:11076 | (1) For the purposes of this Part an interest in shares may arise from an agreement between two or more persons that includes provision for the acquisition by any one or more of them of interests in shares of a particular public company (the “target company” for that agreement).
@ref s 824(1) Interest in shares: agreement to acquire interests in a particular company (src:11076-11076)
GIVEN `the agreement is between two or more persons` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the agreement includes provision for the acquisition by any one or more of them of interests in shares of a particular public company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 824(1) an interest in shares may arise from the agreement` MEANS
    IF `the agreement is between two or more persons` AND `the agreement includes provision for the acquisition by any one or more of them of interests in shares of a particular public company`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "an interest in shares may arise from an agreement between two or more persons that includes provision for the acquisition by any one or more of them of interests in shares of a particular public company"

-- src:11077 | (2) This section applies to such an agreement if—
-- src:11078 | (a) the agreement includes provision imposing obligations or restrictions on any one or more of the parties to it with respect to their use, retention or disposal of their interests in the shares of the target company acquired in pursuance of the agreement (whether or not together with any other interests of theirs in the company's shares to which the agreement relates), and
-- src:11079 | (b) an interest in the target company's shares is in fact acquired by any of the parties in pursuance of the agreement.
@ref s 824(2) Interest in shares: agreement to acquire interests in a particular company (src:11077-11079)
GIVEN `the agreement is one of the kind described in subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the agreement includes provision imposing obligations or restrictions on any one or more of the parties with respect to their use, retention or disposal of their interests in the shares of the target company acquired in pursuance of the agreement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an interest in the target company's shares is in fact acquired by any of the parties in pursuance of the agreement` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 824(2) this section applies to the agreement` MEANS
    IF     `the agreement is one of the kind described in subsection (1)`
       AND `the agreement includes provision imposing obligations or restrictions on any one or more of the parties with respect to their use, retention or disposal of their interests in the shares of the target company acquired in pursuance of the agreement`
       AND `an interest in the target company's shares is in fact acquired by any of the parties in pursuance of the agreement`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section applies to such an agreement if— (a) the agreement includes provision imposing obligations or restrictions ... and (b) an interest in the target company's shares is in fact acquired by any of the parties in pursuance of the agreement."

DECLARE `s 824(3) act` IS ONE OF
    `s 824(3) exercising a right arising from the interests`
    `s 824(3) exercising control or influence arising from the interests`
    `s 824(3) entering into an agreement for the exercise, or for control of the exercise, of any of those rights by another person`
    `s 824(3) another act`

-- src:11080 | (3) The reference in subsection (2) to the use of interests in shares in the target company is to the exercise of any rights or of any control or influence arising from those interests (including the right to enter into an agreement for the exercise, or for control of the exercise, of any of those rights by another person).
@ref s 824(3) Interest in shares: agreement to acquire interests in a particular company (src:11080-11080)
GIVEN act IS A `s 824(3) act`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 824(3) the use of interests in shares includes the act` MEANS
    CONSIDER act
    WHEN `s 824(3) exercising a right arising from the interests` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 824(3) exercising control or influence arising from the interests` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 824(3) entering into an agreement for the exercise, or for control of the exercise, of any of those rights by another person` THEN JUST TRUE
    OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The reference in subsection (2) to the use of interests in shares in the target company is to the exercise of any rights or of any control or influence arising from those interests": a closed meaning ("is to")

-- src:11081 | (4) Once an interest in shares in the target company has been acquired in pursuance of the agreement, this section continues to apply to the agreement so long as the agreement continues to include provisions of any description mentioned in subsection (2).
-- src:11082 | This applies irrespective of—
-- src:11083 | (a) whether or not any further acquisitions of interests in the company's shares take place in pursuance of the agreement;
-- src:11084 | (b) any change in the persons who are for the time being parties to it;
-- src:11085 | (c) any variation of the agreement.
-- src:11086 | References in this subsection to the agreement include any agreement having effect (whether directly or indirectly) in substitution for the original agreement.
@ref s 824(4) Interest in shares: agreement to acquire interests in a particular company (src:11081-11086)
GIVEN `an interest in shares in the target company has been acquired in pursuance of the agreement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the agreement continues to include provisions of any description mentioned in subsection (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 824(4) this section continues to apply to the agreement` MEANS
    IF `an interest in shares in the target company has been acquired in pursuance of the agreement` AND `the agreement continues to include provisions of any description mentioned in subsection (2)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Once an interest in shares in the target company has been acquired in pursuance of the agreement, this section continues to apply to the agreement so long as the agreement continues to include provisions of any description mentioned in subsection (2)."

DECLARE `s 824(4) circumstance` IS ONE OF
    `s 824(4)(a) whether or not any further acquisitions of interests in the company's shares take place in pursuance of the agreement`
    `s 824(4)(b) any change in the persons who are for the time being parties to it`
    `s 824(4)(c) any variation of the agreement`
    `s 824(4) another circumstance`

@ref s 824(4) Interest in shares: agreement to acquire interests in a particular company (src:11082-11085)
GIVEN circumstance IS A `s 824(4) circumstance`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 824(4) it is immaterial to the continued application of this section whether the circumstance occurs` MEANS
    CONSIDER circumstance
    WHEN `s 824(4)(a) whether or not any further acquisitions of interests in the company's shares take place in pursuance of the agreement` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 824(4)(b) any change in the persons who are for the time being parties to it` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 824(4)(c) any variation of the agreement` THEN JUST TRUE
    OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "This applies irrespective of— (a) ... (b) ... (c) ...": the three are named; any other circumstance is not mentioned

@ref s 824(4) Interest in shares: agreement to acquire interests in a particular company (src:11086-11086)
GIVEN `the other agreement has effect (whether directly or indirectly) in substitution for the original agreement` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 824(4) a reference in subsection (4) to the agreement includes the other agreement` MEANS
    IF `the other agreement has effect (whether directly or indirectly) in substitution for the original agreement`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "References in this subsection to the agreement include any agreement having effect (whether directly or indirectly) in substitution for the original agreement."

-- src:11087 | (5) In this section—
-- src:11088 | (a) “agreement” includes any agreement or arrangement, and
-- src:11089 | (b) references to provisions of an agreement include—
-- src:11090 | (i) undertakings, expectations or understandings operative under an arrangement, and
-- src:11091 | (ii) any provision whether express or implied and whether absolute or not.
-- src:11092 | References elsewhere in this Part to an agreement to which this section applies have a corresponding meaning.
@ref s 824(5) Interest in shares: agreement to acquire interests in a particular company (src:11087-11092)
GIVEN `the arrangement is an agreement or arrangement` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 824(5)(a) the arrangement is an agreement` MEANS
    IF `the arrangement is an agreement or arrangement`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "“agreement” includes any agreement or arrangement" does not close the meaning

@ref s 824(5)(b) Interest in shares: agreement to acquire interests in a particular company (src:11089-11091)
GIVEN `the provision is an undertaking, expectation or understanding operative under an arrangement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the provision is express or implied, absolute or not` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 824(5)(b) the provision is a provision of the agreement` MEANS
    IF `the provision is an undertaking, expectation or understanding operative under an arrangement` OR `the provision is express or implied, absolute or not`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "references to provisions of an agreement include— (i) undertakings, expectations or understandings operative under an arrangement, and (ii) any provision whether express or implied and whether absolute or not"

@ref s 824(5) Interest in shares: agreement to acquire interests in a particular company (src:11092-11092)
GIVEN `the reference is a reference elsewhere in this Part to an agreement to which this section applies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 824(5) the reference has a corresponding meaning` MEANS
    IF `the reference is a reference elsewhere in this Part to an agreement to which this section applies`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "References elsewhere in this Part to an agreement to which this section applies have a corresponding meaning."

-- src:11093 | (6) This section does not apply—
-- src:11094 | (a) to an agreement that is not legally binding unless it involves mutuality in the undertakings, expectations or understandings of the parties to it; or
-- src:11095 | (b) to an agreement to underwrite or sub-underwrite an offer of shares in a company, provided the agreement is confined to that purpose and any matters incidental to it.
@ref s 824(6) Interest in shares: agreement to acquire interests in a particular company (src:11093-11095)
GIVEN `the agreement is legally binding` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the agreement involves mutuality in the undertakings, expectations or understandings of the parties to it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 824(6)(a) this section does not apply to the agreement` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the agreement is legally binding` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "This section does not apply— (a) to an agreement that is not legally binding": a legally binding agreement is not mentioned
        IF `the agreement involves mutuality in the undertakings, expectations or understandings of the parties to it` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless it involves mutuality in the undertakings, expectations or understandings of the parties to it" (an "unless" met: fork register)
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

@ref s 824(6)(b) Interest in shares: agreement to acquire interests in a particular company (src:11095-11095)
GIVEN `the agreement is to underwrite or sub-underwrite an offer of shares in a company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the agreement is confined to that purpose and any matters incidental to it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 824(6)(b) this section does not apply to the agreement` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `the agreement is to underwrite or sub-underwrite an offer of shares in a company`) THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "This section does not apply— ... (b) to an agreement to underwrite or sub-underwrite an offer of shares in a company": another agreement is not mentioned
        IF `the agreement is confined to that purpose and any matters incidental to it` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "provided the agreement is confined to that purpose and any matters incidental to it"

§§ `s 825 Extent of obligation in case of share acquisition agreement`

-- src:11097 | (1) For the purposes of this Part each party to an agreement to which section 824 applies is treated as interested in all shares in the target company in which any other party to the agreement is interested apart from the agreement (whether or not the interest of the other party was acquired, or includes any interest that was acquired, in pursuance of the agreement).
@ref s 825(1) Extent of obligation in case of share acquisition agreement (src:11097-11097)
GIVEN `the agreement is one to which section 824 applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a party to the agreement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the shares are shares in the target company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `another party to the agreement is interested in the shares apart from the agreement` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 825(1) the person is treated as interested in the shares` MEANS
    IF     `the agreement is one to which section 824 applies`
       AND `the person is a party to the agreement`
       AND `the shares are shares in the target company`
       AND `another party to the agreement is interested in the shares apart from the agreement`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "each party to an agreement to which section 824 applies is treated as interested in all shares in the target company in which any other party to the agreement is interested apart from the agreement"

-- src:11098 | (2) For those purposes an interest of a party to such an agreement in shares in the target company is an interest apart from the agreement if he is interested in those shares otherwise than by virtue of the application of section 824 (and this section) in relation to the agreement.
@ref s 825(2) Extent of obligation in case of share acquisition agreement (src:11098-11098)
GIVEN `the party is interested in those shares otherwise than by virtue of the application of section 824 (and this section) in relation to the agreement` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 825(2) the interest of the party in shares in the target company is an interest apart from the agreement` MEANS
    IF `the party is interested in those shares otherwise than by virtue of the application of section 824 (and this section) in relation to the agreement`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "an interest of a party to such an agreement in shares in the target company is an interest apart from the agreement if he is interested in those shares otherwise than by virtue of the application of section 824 (and this section) in relation to the agreement"

-- src:11099 | (3) Accordingly, any such interest of the person (apart from the agreement) includes for those purposes any interest treated as his under section 822 or 823 (family or corporate interests) or by the application of section 824 (and this section) in relation to any other agreement with respect to shares in the target company to which he is a party.
@ref s 825(3) Extent of obligation in case of share acquisition agreement (src:11099-11099)
GIVEN `the interest is treated as the person's under section 822 or 823 (family or corporate interests)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the interest is treated as the person's by the application of section 824 (and this section) in relation to any other agreement with respect to shares in the target company to which he is a party` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 825(3) the interest is included in the interest of the person apart from the agreement` MEANS
    IF     `the interest is treated as the person's under section 822 or 823 (family or corporate interests)`
        OR `the interest is treated as the person's by the application of section 824 (and this section) in relation to any other agreement with respect to shares in the target company to which he is a party`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "any such interest of the person (apart from the agreement) includes for those purposes any interest treated as his under section 822 or 823 ... or by the application of section 824 ... in relation to any other agreement" does not close the list

-- src:11100 | (4) A notification with respect to his interest in shares in the target company made to the company under this Part by a person who is for the time being a party to an agreement to which section 824 applies must—
-- src:11101 | (a) state that the person making the notification is a party to such an agreement,
-- src:11102 | (b) include the names and (so far as known to him) the addresses of the other parties to the agreement, identifying them as such, and
-- src:11103 | (c) state whether or not any of the shares to which the notification relates are shares in which he is interested by virtue of section 824 (and this section) and, if so, the number of those shares.
@ref s 825(4) Extent of obligation in case of share acquisition agreement (src:11100-11103)
GIVEN `the notification states that the person making it is a party to such an agreement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notification includes the names and (so far as known to him) the addresses of the other parties to the agreement, identifying them as such` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notification states whether or not any of the shares to which it relates are shares in which he is interested by virtue of section 824 (and this section)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `some of the shares to which the notification relates are shares in which he is interested by virtue of section 824 (and this section)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notification states the number of those shares` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 825(4) the notification contains what the subsection requires` MEANS
    IF     `the notification states that the person making it is a party to such an agreement`
       AND `the notification includes the names and (so far as known to him) the addresses of the other parties to the agreement, identifying them as such`
       AND `the notification states whether or not any of the shares to which it relates are shares in which he is interested by virtue of section 824 (and this section)`
       AND (   (NOT `some of the shares to which the notification relates are shares in which he is interested by virtue of section 824 (and this section)`)
            OR `the notification states the number of those shares`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A notification ... must— (a) state that the person making the notification is a party to such an agreement, (b) include the names and (so far as known to him) the addresses of the other parties ..., and (c) state whether or not any of the shares ... are shares in which he is interested by virtue of section 824 (and this section) and, if so, the number of those shares."

§§ `s 826 Information protected from wider disclosure`

-- src:11106 | (1) Information in respect of which a company is for the time being entitled to any exemption conferred by regulations under section 409(3) (information about related undertakings to be given in notes to accounts: exemption where disclosure harmful to company's business)—
-- src:11107 | (a) must not be included in a report under section 805 (report to members on outcome of investigation), and
-- src:11108 | (b) must not be made available under section 811 (right to inspect and request copy of entries).
