GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 826(2) the fact that the information is omitted must be stated in the report` MEANS
    IF `information of that kind is omitted from a report under section 805`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where any such information is omitted from a report under section 805, that fact must be stated in the report."

§§ `s 827 Reckoning of periods for fulfilling obligations`

-- "Where the period allowed by any provision of this Part for fulfilling an obligation is expressed as a number of days, any
-- day that is not a working day shall be disregarded in reckoning that period."
-- src:11110 | 827 Reckoning of periods for fulfilling obligations
-- src:11111 | Where the period allowed by any provision of this Part for fulfilling an obligation is expressed as a number of days, any day that is not a working day shall be disregarded in reckoning that period.
@ref s 827 Reckoning of periods for fulfilling obligations (src:11110-11111)
GIVEN `the period allowed by a provision of this Part for fulfilling an obligation is expressed as a number of days` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 827 a day that is not a working day is disregarded in reckoning the period` MEANS
    IF `the period allowed by a provision of this Part for fulfilling an obligation is expressed as a number of days`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where the period allowed by any provision of this Part for fulfilling an obligation is expressed as a number of days": a period in weeks, months or years is not mentioned

-- The stepper: the last day of a period of n days that starts after `start`. The first day counted is the day after `start`.
-- Whether a day is a working day is the keel's rule (s 1173(1), "working day"), which this part does not import: the caller
-- passes it as a function from a date to BOOLEAN.
@ref s 827 Reckoning of periods for fulfilling obligations (src:11111-11111)
GIVEN start IS A DATE
      n IS A NUMBER
      `s 1173(1) the day is a working day for the company` IS A FUNCTION FROM DATE TO BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DATE
`s 827 the last day of a period of days counting only working days` MEANS
    step start n
    WHERE
        GIVEN d IS A DATE, k IS A NUMBER
        GIVETH A DATE
        step MEANS
            IF k AT MOST 0
            THEN d
            ELSE IF `s 1173(1) the day is a working day for the company` (Date (Day d PLUS 1))
                 THEN step (Date (Day d PLUS 1)) (k MINUS 1)
                 ELSE step (Date (Day d PLUS 1)) k

-- The count: the number of working days after `from`, up to and including `to`.
@ref s 827 Reckoning of periods for fulfilling obligations (src:11111-11111)
GIVEN from IS A DATE
      to IS A DATE
      `s 1173(1) the day is a working day for the company` IS A FUNCTION FROM DATE TO BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 827 the number of working days after one date up to and including another` MEANS
    count from 0
    WHERE
        GIVEN d IS A DATE, acc IS A NUMBER
        GIVETH A NUMBER
        count MEANS
            IF Day d LESS THAN Day to
            THEN count (Date (Day d PLUS 1)) (IF `s 1173(1) the day is a working day for the company` (Date (Day d PLUS 1)) THEN acc PLUS 1 ELSE acc)
            ELSE acc

